<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50838" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππότης</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>driver</i> or <i>rider of horses, horseman, knight</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.55
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				9.49
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				69
			</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always in 
				Ep.
			 nom. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππότᾰ</span>, as <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γερήνιος ἱππότα Νέστωρ</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.336
			</span></i>, etc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππότης Κολωνός</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				59
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππότης</span></b> 
			<i>on</i>
			<i>horseback</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tox.</u>
				47
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὶ ἱππότη</span>, 
				Boeot.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἱππεῖς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.3087
			</span></i> (Lebad.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				10.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππόται λαοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.153
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. λεώς</span>
			<i>the horse</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				80
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεὼν ἄνιππον ἱ. τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					899
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. ὄχλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					660
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Aem.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			.—Never used in correct 
				Att.
			 Prose.</div>
